# Attachment Theory

According to attachment theory, there are different styles of attachment, learned by individuals during childhood, based on their 
relationships with their primary caregivers. These styles affect how individuals form and maintain relationships throughout their life.

As children grow, they use their attachment figures as a secure base from which to explore the world and to return to for comfort.

The 4 attachment styles are: 

1) Secure attachment
    
2) Anxious attachment
3) Avoidant attachment
4) Disorganized attachment

